From 72dbda57332468244058f35ae506f0aa78d87c04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Dean <galdre@galdorcraeft.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:59:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add a local mode that explains a commit range in a local
 repository

The --local option reads a commit range (--base, --head) in a local git
repository (--repo), with a title (--title) and an optional description
(--body-file). Tulip then needs no GitHub pull request and no network access
to GitHub. The diff and the file list come from git diff. The checkout is a
detached git worktree of the local repository in a temporary directory, and
cleanup removes that worktree. Local mode refuses --serve, because --serve
posts comments to GitHub.
---
